# Code owners for the paths that touch patient health information.
#
# master's branch protection currently requires one approving review from any
# collaborator, with require_code_owner_reviews disabled. That means a diff to
# the AI agent tool allowlist, the patient profile service, or a database
# migration can be approved by whoever is around, on exactly the same terms as
# a README typo. This file is the input GitHub needs before that setting can be
# turned on.
#
# BEFORE ENABLING require_code_owner_reviews: add a second maintainer to the
# PHI blocks below. Every entry today is @fjiexiao, who authors nearly every
# commit in this repository, and GitHub does not let a pull request author
# satisfy their own code-owner review — flipping the setting with a single
# owner listed would block that author's own PRs outright.

# Default owner. More specific rules below win; the last matching line wins in
# CODEOWNERS, so the PHI paths are listed after this one.
*                                       @fjiexiao

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# PHI paths. A change here can leak or corrupt a patient's medical record.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# AI agent tooling: the retrievers, the prompt allowlist, the PII redactor and
# the renderer that decides what leaves the process and reaches a model.
/apps/api/src/modules/ai-agents/         @fjiexiao

# Patient profile and document handling: reads, writes and deletes of the
# records themselves.
/apps/api/src/modules/patient-profile/   @fjiexiao

# Authentication and OTP: the only thing standing between a phone number and
# somebody else's medical history.
/apps/api/src/modules/auth/              @fjiexiao
/apps/api/src/services/otp/              @fjiexiao

# Schema changes. Migrations are applied automatically on every api container
# start, and several down scripts are destructive by nature — 016's own header
# warns that dropping deleted_at resurrects every retracted follow-up record.
/db/migrations/                          @fjiexiao
/db/init_db.sql                          @fjiexiao

# The OCR and report-parsing layer. Its failure mode is not a crash but a
# structured field that is confidently wrong, which the API's prompt allowlist
# then treats as trusted input.
/apps/report-manager/                    @fjiexiao
/apps/api/src/services/ocr/              @fjiexiao

# The gate itself. Weakening CI, the owner list, or the release process should
# not be reviewable by someone other than an owner.
/.github/                                @fjiexiao
